out←queryParams(_con sql params);stmt
⍝ Prepare, bind, and execute a parameterized query in one call
⍝ _con: connection pointer
⍝ sql: SQL query with parameters ($1, $2, etc.)
⍝ params: vector of parameter values
⍝ Returns: query results (same format as query function) or error message

stmt←prepareQuery _con sql
:If stmt=0
    out←'Failed to prepare statement' ⋄ →0
:EndIf

:If 0=stmt bindParams params
    {}destroyPrepared stmt
    out←'Failed to bind parameters' ⋄ →0
:EndIf

out←executePrepared stmt
{}destroyPrepared stmt

